#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/witch-hunters.adoc:41
msgid ""
"image:witch-hunters/logo.webp[width=109,height=108,float=\"right\"] Witch "
"Hunters are some of the most characterful and interesting aspects of the "
"Empire. While it’s true to say they invariably fight for the greater good of "
"humanity, their methods are often brutal and arguably little better than "
"those of their enemies. A Witch Hunter knows that evil doesn’t play by the "
"rules however, and that to beat it, he must be just as underhand. If a few "
"innocents get killed in the process, then it’s regrettable but better than "
"allowing a heretic or warlock to escape punishment."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/witch-hunters.adoc:56
msgid ""
"Often, Witch Hunters prefer to work alone or in small groups, such as during "
"the scouring of Mordheim years ago.  Occasionally though there will be need "
"to gather together under one banner to drive out some great, dark army. "
"Probably the two most famous times were during the last Great Chaos "
"Incursion, when a Witch Hunter army was lead by Magnus the Pious; and during "
"the Wars of the Vampire Counts, when the whole Empire united to defend "
"itself against the armies of Vlad and Mannfred Von Carstein. At times like "
"these, Witch Hunters stir up support from the mobs, and priests take up the "
"hammer, leading their congregation to defend the lands.  Flagellants seem "
"drawn to these gatherings like flies, preaching damnation and hellfire "
"almost as loudly as the Witch Hunters themselves."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/witch-hunters.adoc:76
msgid ""
"Of course, it does not take a desperate situation such as a Chaos incursion "
"to cause this. Quite often, a Witch Hunter will find need to gather a force "
"to eradicate a tribe of beastmen in a surrounding forest, or cast out a "
"Necrarch from a dark tower in the mountains. If the local noble has not the "
"time, or more likely the inclination, it calls to a Witch Hunter to deal "
"with it. He may have some aid in the form of the town watch or soldiers of "
"the merchants guild, or even a detachment of one of the Knightly Orders, but "
"often this is not the case.  A Witch Hunter’s army is a rag-tag sight. The "
"black garbed Zealots of the Witch Hunters’ guild stand shoulder-to-shoulder "
"with peasants and hastily gathered watchmen. Packs of Warhounds, equally "
"trained to seek out the scent of the Undead or a heretic, follow baying and "
"howling. Occasionally a regiment of Knights marches ahead, their bright "
"armour contrasts to the rags of the army’s bulk. Priests continue their "
"sermons on the battlefield, encouraging their followers to acts of insane "
"bravery, while frothing Flagellants whip themselves for the sins they may "
"have committed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/witch-hunters.adoc:81
#, no-wrap
msgid "Witch Hunter army selector"
msgstr ""

#. type: Table
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/witch-hunters.adoc:86
#, no-wrap
msgid "include::partial$witch-hunters.tsv[]\n"
msgstr ""

#.  Add the, the
#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/witch-hunters.adoc:100
msgid ""
"Some unit’s abilities from Witch Hunter army will affect ‘Chaos and/or "
"Undead’. ‘Chaos’ means the Chaos army, Daemons army, Beastmen army, Chaos "
"Dwarf army and Skaven army. ‘Undead’ means the Tomb Kings army and Vampire "
"Counts army (including units of Ghouls!)."
msgstr ""

#. 2: + moved
#. 3: they'll → Flagellants
#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/witch-hunters.adoc:108
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[zealots,†1]]1. Zealots"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/witch-hunters.adoc:113
msgid ""
"Zealots form the main part of a Witch Hunter army, and are drawn from mobs "
"whipped up by priest’s sermons.  These troops gain +1 Attack in the first "
"round of combat against Undead or Chaos (regardless of who charged) and will "
"always use their initiative to charge these enemies if possible."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/witch-hunters.adoc:117
msgid ""
"If victorious in combat with Undead or Chaos like enemies they must pursue "
"or advance where possible."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/witch-hunters.adoc:122
msgid ""
"Count enemy Armour values as one worse than normal when shot by a handgun. "
"So an armour value of 3+ counts as 4+, 4+ as 5+, and 5+ as 6+, whilst an "
"Armour value of 6+ can’t save against a handgun."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/witch-hunters.adoc:123
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[flagellants,†3]]3. Flagellants"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/witch-hunters.adoc:131
msgid ""
"So keen are they to meet their maker that a unit of Flagellants will always "
"use its initiative to charge an enemy if possible and can’t be given orders "
"instead. Flagellants never use their initiative to evade. They can’t be "
"driven back by shooting and do not roll for drive backs. If victorious in "
"combat they must pursue or advance where possible. Flagellants are "
"unaffected by enemies that cause terror in combat, so they do not suffer the "
"usual −1 Attack modifier."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/witch-hunters.adoc:132
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[warhounds,†4]]4. Warhounds"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/witch-hunters.adoc:139
msgid ""
"Warhound stands are not deployed as independent units. Instead, any infantry "
"unit may add one stand of Warhounds. This brings the size of the unit to 4 "
"stands; 3 regular stands plus the Warhound stand. Warhounds always have the "
"same Armour value as the rest of their unit. They fight as part of their "
"unit and can be removed as a unit casualty if the player wishes."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/witch-hunters.adoc:141
msgid "Warhound casualties never count for Command penalties."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/witch-hunters.adoc:146
msgid ""
"Warhound stands never cause the parent unit to be in Irregular Formation no "
"matter how they are placed. An Infantry unit containing a Warhound stand "
"gains the ability to pursue Cavalry and Chariots."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/witch-hunters.adoc:147
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[pistoliers,†5]]5. Pistoliers"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/witch-hunters.adoc:152
msgid ""
"Pistoliers have a shooting range of only 15cm and 360° vision – stands in "
"this unit can draw line of sight from all edges for the purpose of evading "
"and shooting, including shooting at charging enemies. Note that this unit "
"still needs Line of Sight from its front edge to charge an enemy."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/witch-hunters.adoc:153
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[cannons,†6]]6. Cannons"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/witch-hunters.adoc:155
msgid ""
"See the rules for xref:rules:artillery-and-machines.adoc#cannons[Cannons] in "
"the Warmaster Rulebook."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/witch-hunters.adoc:160
#, no-wrap
msgid "Witch Hunter spells"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/witch-hunters.adoc:163
#, no-wrap
msgid "Sanctuary"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/witch-hunters.adoc:169
msgid ""
"_The Warrior Priest consecrates the ground before the troops, warding off "
"evil._"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/witch-hunters.adoc:176
msgid ""
"The Wizard must be with the unit to affect it. The unit counts as being "
"defended, even if in the open. If the unit is already defended, it counts as "
"fortified. Note that this also affects Cavalry units, even though they are "
"not normally able to receive this bonus. The effect lasts until the unit "
"moves or Priest leaves it or he casts another spell."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/witch-hunters.adoc:178
#, no-wrap
msgid "Doctrine of Sigmar"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/witch-hunters.adoc:184
msgid ""
"_Through the rousting speech of Sigmar’s chosen, troops are directed across "
"the field of battle._"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/witch-hunters.adoc:189
msgid ""
"The spell can be cast on any unengaged friendly unit within range regardless "
"of whether the Priest can see it or not. The spell affects only a single "
"unit, never a brigade and there is no supporting charge possible."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/witch-hunters.adoc:195
#, no-wrap
msgid "Holy Fervour"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/witch-hunters.adoc:201
msgid ""
"_Enraged by their blasphemous enemies the troops rush forward thirsty for "
"blood._"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/witch-hunters.adoc:205
msgid ""
"The Wizard must be with the unit to affect it. If successfully cast on a "
"friendly unit, each stand including character stands gains +1 Attack during "
"the following Combat phase."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/witch-hunters.adoc:207
#, no-wrap
msgid "Divine Curse"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/witch-hunters.adoc:213
msgid ""
"_Speaking the words of Magnus the Pious himself, the Warrior Priest smites "
"his foes._"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/witch-hunters.adoc:217
msgid ""
"This spell can be cast on any enemy unit within range regardless of whether "
"the Priest can see it or not. The spell lasts until the end of the opposing "
"player’s following turn."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/witch-hunters.adoc:226
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/partials/empire-spells.adoc:64
msgid ""
"The unit moves at half pace in all situations: even when charging for "
"example. The unit counts all enemies as terrifying (−1 Attack penalty) even "
"when it is otherwise immune to terror. If the unit would normally cause "
"terror then it ceases to do so and counts all enemies as terrifying just "
"like everyone else. However, if the target is Undead or Daemon it will not "
"count enemies as terrifying although all other penalties apply as described "
"(Undead and Daemons are hard to spook)."
msgstr ""
